 "limits": "Static evidence only: byte pins, relocation bindings, and find-based censuses validated as instruction starts for every asserted site inside a packet owner. No captured code was executed. Semantic names (spec, value, ctx, temp, registry) follow the earlier RE-005 packets and the byte-level roles proven here; no type names are claimed.",
 "map_layout": {
  "entry": "stride 0x48: key ptr +0x0, key len +0x8, value record (0x38 bytes) at +0x10; value +0x20 = value-object pointer, value +0x28 = getter presence word, value +0x30 = counter word",
  "getter_read": "items gate [map +0x30]; hash 0x4e52640 over state at map +0x38; on a key match the presence word at entry +0x38 must be nonzero, then the string is ([object +0x8], [object +0x10]) of the object at entry +0x30",
  "table_header": "standalone form (temp): buckets +0x0, mask +0x8, growth-left +0x10, items +0x18, hash state +0x20",
  "value": "0x50 bytes: prefix +0x0..+0x18; table header at +0x18 (buckets +0x18, mask +0x20, growth-left +0x28, items +0x30); hash state +0x38 (16 bytes); inner pointer +0x48"
 },
 "next_question": "For path A, which of the worker's frame-struct builders \u2014 or the delegated final assembly 0x164df60 \u2014 first writes a chain entry into a value-layout table, and can the ctx table the worker's get-or-insert pass counts spec names into be the same table the result is later copied from? For path B, who first writes a chain key into the registry ctx the builder merges from, or into the spec entry array the pairs are taken from?",
