 "path_a_registry_worker": {
  "get_or_insert_sites": "0x16327b9 (spec entry name key) and 0x163281e (per-element string keys, loop); both pass the ctx (arg3, saved at [rsp+0x30]) as the map \u2014 never the result pointer saved at [rsp+0x58]. Two dedicated counter callees reach the same helper: entry_counter_a 0x162cee0 at its site 0x162cf0b (map = its arg4, which the worker fills with the ctx at 0x1631e42; key from its arg3 +0x78/+0x80) and entry_counter_b 0x163a070 at its site 0x163a239 (map = its first stack argument, which the worker stores the ctx into at 0x1631c7f; key = the spec entry name at +0x170/+0x178). A whole-binary census of slot 0x64e1ba8 finds exactly these four call sites",
  "insert_into_result": "none: no direct or slot call to the shared insert-or-replace 0x1669390 anywhere in the worker body, and no worker callee reaches it except get-or-insert 0x1667540",
  "inserted_default": "the get-or-insert default record has word 0 at value +0x28, so the getter presence gate would reject any entry it creates; its counter word at value +0x30 starts at 1 and is incremented on a hit",
  "remove_op_sites": "0x16317bf, 0x1632743, 0x1634350 \u2014 all pass the ctx as first argument; the helper deletes ctx entries (items decrement at ctx +0x30, growth-left increment at ctx +0x28, tombstone control bytes)",
  "result_writes": "direct field stores from frame-local structs at the exit sites pinned in the packet (items word [result +0x30], buckets word [result +0x18], and block copies), plus the delegated final-assembly call at 0x16343d1 (slot 0x64e1cb8 -> 0x164df60, hash-pinned boundary) with (result, three frame structs, ctx)",
  "verdict": "the chain entry is not inserted into the result map inside the registry worker body; the worker's only map inserts target the ctx, with spec-derived keys and a counter default value the getter cannot read as a string"
 },
 "path_b_merge_builder": {
  "base_case": "pair count == 0 or ctx items == 0 -> 0x1667d63: with an inner pointer at [ctx +0x48], a local header is built from the template at 0x6407558/0x6407568 and the inner pointee's fields, its [inner +0x18] word is set to the sentinel, the builder recurses (0x1667e3d), and the resulting fields are swapped back; with no inner pointer it falls straight into the drain",
  "drain_insert": "site 0x1668034 -> 0x1669390 with map header = ctx +0x18 (r12 advanced by the single +0x18 add at 0x1667ee6, saved/restored through [rsp+0x28]), key = the temp entry's own key ptr/len (saved at 0x1667f62/0x1667f6c), value = the temp entry's value copied via 0x16595d0 at 0x1667fd9; the displaced old value's head is compared against the sentinel at 0x166804f and dropped when different",
  "pair_insert": "site 0x1667c0e -> 0x1669390 with map = temp ([rsp+0x38]), key = the pair's own (ptr, len), value record built at rsp+0xb8 from the ctx/temp entries via the value copy helper 0x16595d0; reached only below the ctx-match fall-through (bcmp at 0x1667868, je at 0x1667870): a ctx miss exits through the empty-group edge at 0x16678b8 to the next-pair edge 0x1667ca0 with no insert",
  "verdict": "the builder never creates a key and never references the chain key bytes at 0x92a7be; a chain entry reaches the getter's map in path B only through the drain insert at 0x1668034, and only if the temp table holds a chain entry at drain time \u2014 pre-existing from the core-built temp, or staged by the pair loop when a spec pair's key is \"chain\" and \"chain\" is already present in the ctx"
 },
